# Part Tracking tag URLs: serve the resolver page for every /p/<part_id>.
# Cloudflare Pages rewrites run BEFORE static asset lookup — the old comment
# claiming Netlify-style "static files take precedence" was wrong here. The
# previous rule (/p/* /p/index.html 200) was silently dropped by Cloudflare's
# parseRedirects infinite-loop guard (target matched its own /p/* source),
# 404ing every tag URL in production (R21-10). Rewriting to /p/ serves the
# directory index without tripping the guard. Published JSON mirrors live
# under /p-records/ so this rewrite cannot shadow them.
/p/* /p/ 200
